mothershipOS: the external camera HAL takes uncompressed V4L2_PIX_FMT_XBGR32 (BGRx) frames besides MJPEG, the format
a mothershipOS host gives its VMs' cameras (mship.camera): probed and advertised as a color format, converted to
YU12 with libyuv::ARGBToI420. Without it the HAL rejects every such camera ("Supported formats list is empty").
Its frame size cap allows 4 bytes per pixel (was 3: every XBGR32 frame was dropped as too big).

diff -ruN a/camera/device/default/ExternalCameraDevice.cpp b/camera/device/default/ExternalCameraDevice.cpp
